From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RetroStoneOS <noreply@8bcraft.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] clk: sunxi-ng: a10: register the CCU driver at subsys_initcall

The A10/A20 CCU became a platform driver (module_platform_driver, i.e.
device_initcall), but drivers/pinctrl is linked before drivers/clk. So
at device_initcall time the A20 pin controller is probed first, fw_devlink
sees that its "apb" clock supplier (the CCU) is not bound yet and defers
it, and deferred probes are only retried from late_initcall on
(deferred_probe_initcall). Everything that needs pins (the SD card, I2C
and the PMIC, the UARTs, the display) then probes from the late_initcall
flush onwards: on the RetroStone2 the pin controller probed at 0.199 s and
the SD host at 0.309 s instead of about 0.1 s, which delayed the root
filesystem mount and /sbin/init.

Register the driver at subsys_initcall. The platform devices exist since
arch_initcall_sync (of_platform_default_populate_init), and the CCU's own
suppliers are the fixed 24 MHz and 32 kHz oscillators (CLK_OF_DECLARE), so
it binds at once and every consumer finds it bound at device_initcall.
---
 drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun4i-a10.c | 13 ++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun4i-a10.c b/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun4i-a10.c
--- a/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun4i-a10.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun4i-a10.c
@@ -1491,7 +1491,17 @@
 		.of_match_table		= sun4i_a10_ccu_ids,
 	},
 };
-module_platform_driver(sun4i_a10_ccu_driver);
+
+/*
+ * Before device_initcall: the pin controller (drivers/pinctrl is linked
+ * before drivers/clk) and every other consumer must find the CCU bound,
+ * or fw_devlink defers them until late_initcall.
+ */
+static int __init sun4i_a10_ccu_init(void)
+{
+	return platform_driver_register(&sun4i_a10_ccu_driver);
+}
+subsys_initcall(sun4i_a10_ccu_init);

 MODULE_IMPORT_NS("SUNXI_CCU");
 MODULE_DESCRIPTION("Support for the Allwinner A10/A20 CCU");
--
2.43.0
